-- title:
--   Adelic box of D∩ gwidehatΛ equals gwidehatΛ
-- statement:
--   Let $D$ be a ring equipped with a $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra structure and let $\Lambda$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ which is finitely generated and whose $\mathbb{Q}$-span is all of $D$; thus $\Lambda$ is a full $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice in $D$. For a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule $M$ of $D$, write $\widehat{M} :=$ [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox M`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) for the additive subgroup of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$ generated by the pure tensors $z \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} a$ with $z \in M$ and $a$ a finite adele of $\mathbb{Q}$ that lies in the valuation ring $v$-adically for every height one prime $v$ of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$, where the finite adele ring is formed with respect to $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $g$ be a unit of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$, and let [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele Λ g`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) be the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of $D$ obtained as the preimage of the translate $g \cdot \widehat{\Lambda}$ (the image of $\widehat{\Lambda}$ under left multiplication by $g$) along the map $d \mapsto d \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} 1$, i.e. $D \cap g\widehat{\Lambda}$. The assertion is the equality of additive subgroups of $D \otimes_{\mathbb{Q}} \mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{f}$
--   $$\widehat{\,D \cap g\widehat{\Lambda}\,} \;=\; g\,\widehat{\Lambda}.$$
--
--   This is the local–global dictionary for lattices in a finite-dimensional $\mathbb{Q}$-algebra: every left translate of $\widehat{\Lambda}$ by a finite idele is recovered as the adelic box of the $\mathbb{Z}$-lattice it cuts out in $D$, so that $M \mapsto D \cap M$ and $L \mapsto \widehat{L}$ are mutually inverse on such lattices. It underlies the identification of adelic double cosets with lattice classes used in the Čerednik–Drinfel'd coset graph computations and in the description of Hecke operators at a level.
-- source:
